WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.210
- Hi, I'm Hilary Duff,

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.593
and I'm at BuzzFeed,
here to do an interview.

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:09.103
(Gasps) No, no, no, four puppies?

00:00:10.228 --> 00:00:11.763
Why do I get to do this?

00:00:11.763 --> 00:00:13.481
- [Woman In background] Surprise.

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:15.564
- You smell so delicious.

00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:18.385
Oh my goodness, hi.

00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:23.118
Guys, I'm gonna cry.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.740
You can't answer questions
when there's puppies.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.090
Do you plan on writing any
more books in the future

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.943
and what are you reading nowadays?

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.220
I don't have any plans to write any books.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.140
It was one of the hardest
things I've ever done.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.913
And right now I just finished
a book called Pachinko,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:37.800
which I loved.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.453
It was very ambitious for
me, it was like 500 pages.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.823
And now I'm reading a
book called I See You.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.933
Look at this little floppy body.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.120
What's one childhood teenage experience

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.470
you feel you missed out on?

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.450
I never got to have braces and
I never got to have a locker.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.550
It was two things I
really was desperate for.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.703
Would you ever do a Lizzy McGuire reboot?

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:57.810
Honestly, the idea sounded terrible

00:00:57.810 --> 00:00:59.360
like two years ago when reboots

00:00:59.691 --> 00:01:00.524
(laughs)

00:01:00.524 --> 00:01:02.760
when reboots were happening,
but you never know.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.900
I don't know, I loved,
I loved Lizzy McGuire.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.463
And it might be really fun
to see where she is now.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.243
Hey, get outta my fishbowl.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.730
Do you still know the monologue

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:13.030
from the locker room scene
in A Cinderella Story?

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:14.149
Is it like something about waiting for you

00:01:14.149 --> 00:01:16.217
was like waiting for
the rain in a drought?

00:01:16.217 --> 00:01:17.220
- [Woman In Background] Oh, no.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.288
I've seen little like
memes, that's why I know.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:22.130
If you could have one
normal day to yourself

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:24.389
without any paparazzi or
fans, what would you do?

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:26.259
I'd probably go to the beach.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:28.040
And I would just be with my kid.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.320
We're so used to it now,
but it is not the fans

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.243
but the paparazzi, it
kind of is a bum out.

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.610
So that would be nice to just have a day

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.090
where he's not aware, and I'm not aware

00:01:39.197 --> 00:01:42.213
and we would probably just
go about and do normal stuff.

00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:43.270
Oh god.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.933
Are you Team Josh or Team Charles and why?

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.583
I'm team Josh.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.013
Always team Josh.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.800
Once Charles and Liza finally
bone and get it over with

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.260
like what are they just still gonna talk

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.260
about books all day?

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.240
I wish that you guys could watch this

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.880
and like get the smells as
like additional sensations.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:03.800
It's so cute.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.030
Did you or anyone else ever get
hit with the giant red balls

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.180
in the Lizzie McGuire
opening credit scene?

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.033
Yes, all day long, giant red
balls, just flying at you.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:16.810
At what moment did you realize
you were actually famous?

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.480
Oh, I know the exact moment.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.740
Lizzie McGuire aired
and that weekend I went

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.390
to go meet my friends at the mall

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.100
and I literally had to
hide in a janitor's closet.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.943
It was like the craziest thing.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.450
I had to call my mom from the closet.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.550
Like someone who worked
at the mall was like

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.870
getting me in a closet
and my mom had to come

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.640
and pick me up, it was really crazy.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.030
It was actually a little scary.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.447
You, this tiny little nugget is so feisty.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.160
You and your little
heart is just pounding.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:44.453
You're so cute.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.590
If you had to give your
Younger cast members

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.870
yearbook super- what is super-latives?

00:02:51.096 --> 00:02:53.830
- [Woman In Background]
Superlatives, like in the yearbook-

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.710
- Guys, didn't

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:55.815
- [Woman In Background] like class clowns

00:02:55.815 --> 00:02:57.557
- Didn't go to high school,
I'm like What's that?

00:02:57.557 --> 00:02:58.390
(laughing in background)

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.503
Nico would be the biggest flirt for sure.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:03.023
Miriam would be the class clown.

00:03:03.048 --> 00:03:05.873
I think probably Kelsey
would be like prom queen.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.050
Did I do good enough?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:07.933
Okay.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.100
Which one of your songs
could you listen to

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.616
on repeat and which one would you

00:03:12.616 --> 00:03:14.683
want to erase from your memory?

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:16.290
My boyfriend brought it up the other day.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.660
He was like "You know
what was the best song?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.980
Wake Up, Wake Up was the best song."

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:21.813
It was so cute.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.280
I was like You know that one?

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.830
From the newer album

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:29.730
I love Spark, the single,
it was really fun.

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:32.280
There's a lot on Metamorphosis
that I wish I could forget.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.800
But then so many people come up to me

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.950
and they're like That
album was everything to me.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.190
And they always call out
the most embarrassing songs.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:41.090
Like there's this song called The Math

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.780
and I don't get it at all.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.460
That's like one of my most
embarrassing moments in life.

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:48.590
So, probably a lot from that record.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:49.690
Hard to choose really.

00:03:49.789 --> 00:03:51.628
What is your favorite
Lizzy McGuire episode

00:03:51.628 --> 00:03:54.003
and which episode haunts you to this day?

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.180
My favorite episode is I Want a Bra,

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.220
a Bra, a Bra, a Bra, a Bra.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.610
First of all, I think filming
it was absolutely mortifying

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.060
for me 'cause I probably had just

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.420
gotten a bra in real life anyway.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.780
But when I watch it back,
I like that it's so funny.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.130
What if this went to shit

00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:10.563
and I started getting
beat up on by the puppies?

00:04:10.748 --> 00:04:12.157
(laughing)

00:04:12.157 --> 00:04:14.123
This is like the best thing ever.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:16.097
I think everybody should
get to play with puppies

00:04:16.097 --> 00:04:18.513
no matter what their job.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.113
This is so happy; this is so funny.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.800
Honestly, this was the best treat ever.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.480
Guys, all of these
puppies are for adoption

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.780
through the North Shore
Animal League America.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.623
Who doesn't wanna play with this all day?

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.063
Get your puppies.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.483
Oh my god, this is the best.

